		"notes": "\n\t<p><i>Frail, wispy, child-sized spirit dressed in grey rags, with an animal skull for a head. Surrounded by the tortured sobbing of stolen voices</i></p>\n\t<p></p>\n\t<p><strong>AC</strong> 11, <strong>HP</strong> 19, <strong>ATK</strong> 2 claw +2 (1d4 + fatigue) or steal voice, <strong>MV</strong> near, <strong>S</strong> -1, <strong>D</strong> +1, <strong>C</strong> +1, <strong>I</strong> +0, <strong>W</strong> +0, <strong>Ch</strong> +1, <strong>AL</strong> <strong>C</strong>, <strong>LV</strong> 4</p><p></p>\n\t<p><strong>Fatigue</strong>. CON 12+ or sleep for 1d4 hours, cannot be easily awoken.</p><p></p><p><strong>Greater Undead</strong>. Immune to morale checks. Only damaged by silver or magical sources.</p><p></p><p><strong>Steal Voice</strong>. Steal the voice of an unconscious target, which the whisperer can replicate perfectly.</p><p></p>\n\t<p><i>Shadowfinder Complete Bestiary</i></p>",
